Dirk Zimmermann wrote:
>
> Hmm, doesn't dropbox synch all changed files? Or did you continue on
> another machine while files where still synching?

My speculation not knowing exactly how this sync program works ...

> A trickery happens (to the best of my knowledge) when a level is
> loaded that is "disguised" via filename as another level, or when the
> process ID in the level file doesn't match the one from the restored
> saved game.

If the sync program copies newly created or modified files to the copy
but does not delete newly deleted files from the copy than it will get a
different process ID.

I've had similar happen to me using UNIX "rdist" years ago.  If I set it
to not delete files on the copy crud would build up.  If I set it to
delete files on the copy then I was not protected from accidental
deletions.

> So if you just make sure that after a save, all save files are copied
> to the other machine before you continue playing it should work fine.



